// This pack's own strict typecheck program — self-contained inside
// `packs/riot/`, no path reaching up into core's checkout. Content-pack-
// extraction batch 5 task 6 fix round 2: the previous config,
// `../../tsconfig.pack-riot.json`, lived at core's own repo root and this
// pack's `typecheck` script reached it with a relative `../../` path — the
// same defect Task 5 was found for on a different script, and one that
// resolves to nothing the day this directory is a repository of its own.
//
// `extends` core by its package name, not a relative path, so this file
// keeps working unchanged whether `@moba2d/core` is a workspace symlink
// (today) or a real npm dependency (once this pack is a repository of its
// own). `@moba2d/core/tsconfig.base.json` is the shared compiler-options
// base `tsconfig.json` (core's own root program) also extends — including
// `@/*`, core's own internal alias, resolved relative to *that config
// file's own location* regardless of where this one lives (see its own
// header for why that makes it portable rather than a second `../../` in
// disguise). This pack's own code may still never write `@/...` itself —
// that is the `pack-core-boundary` seam's rule, an import scan this pack's
// own `check-seams` runs over this whole package, not a typecheck one — but
// this pack's compiler needs the alias resolvable
// to see real types *through* `@moba2d/core`'s exported entry points,
// which are core's own unbundled source and import via `@/*` internally
// like the rest of that codebase.
//
// `types` fills the two ambient-declaration gaps that go with it:
// `vite/client` for `generated/assetManifest.ts`'s `'...png?url'` asset
// imports (Vite's own syntax — a real dependency this pack already has
// through the workspace, not something to reach for in core's own copy
// of the reference), and core's `global.d.ts` (p5 in global mode) and
// `poly-decomp.d.ts` (the physics library's own missing types), both
// published the same way `tsconfig.base.json` is.
{
  "extends": "@moba2d/core/tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "strict": true,
    "types": [
      "vite/client",
      "@moba2d/core/types/global.d.ts",
      "@moba2d/core/types/poly-decomp.d.ts"
    ]
  },
  "include": ["**/*.ts"]
}
